module Primitives
    intent =
        "The two primitives Aver has not got, declared as a contract rather"
        "than written."
        "A capability module is a contract with no body: it says what the"
        "operation means and leaves a host to supply it. Both of these are"
        "pure, which is the right shape for a hash and for a curve -- the same"
        "arguments always give the same answer, there is nothing to record and"
        "nothing to replay."
        "They are one contract rather than two because a provider binds a whole"
        "contract. One module means one contract_hash, one provider package and"
        "one line in aver.toml, and there is no case where this project would"
        "want a curve without a hash or the other way round."
        "Octets rather than Bytes because capability contract v1 requires every"
        "boundary type to be declared in the capability module, so that"
        "contract_hash pins its layout. A type borrowed from the stdlib is not"
        "owned, and Aver refuses the contract if one is used. The conversion"
        "at the edge is the price of that, and it is charged in the callers."
        "Nothing here can be checked by aver verify against a real"
        "implementation. A verify case that reaches one of these operations"
        "runs an Aver stub bound with given, which tests what the caller does"
        "with an answer rather than whether the answer is right. Whether it is"
        "right is the provider's own business and is tested in the provider's"
        "own language, against the published vectors, where the implementation"
        "actually is."
    kind = capability
    semantics = pure
    exposes [Octets, ripemd160, verifySignature]

record Octets
    values: List<Int>

operation ripemd160(input: Octets) -> Octets
    ? "The twenty-byte RIPEMD-160 digest of these bytes."
      "Bare RIPEMD-160, not OP_HASH160: the composite is Bitcoin's and is"
      "composed by the caller out of this and the SHA-256 Aver already has."

operation verifySignature(publicKey: Octets, signature: Octets, message: Octets) -> Bool
    ? "Whether this is a valid secp256k1 ECDSA signature by this public key"
      "over this thirty-two byte message."
      "The signature is DER without the trailing hash type byte, and the"
      "message is the signature hash, already computed. False means the"
      "signature does not verify; it does not mean the inputs were malformed,"
      "which the caller refuses before it gets here."
